aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520525 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186520618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520525 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0fd9eb12-d390-5e28-b525-37da4fd463b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520525 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520583 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186520600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520583 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a2108fe-05ce-5a0f-93ec-aefbea01ef7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520583 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186520509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520585 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9110dbbf-595e-5932-adab-f257d78e5fbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520585 #e